Only in this laboratory.

00:33:29.760 --> 00:33:40.360 position:63%
Caiman and his men start now a long, laborious process to transform the coca paste, the raw material form which cocaine is made, into 25 kilos of pure cocaine.

00:33:48.920 --> 00:33:57.120 position:63%
The first part of the process consists of eliminating the impurities of the coca paste, and for this, chemical products are needed.

00:33:59.760 --> 00:34:05.000 position:63%
There is water with sulfuric acid.

00:34:05.000 --> 00:34:06.680 position:63%
Sulfuric acid.

00:34:06.680 --> 00:34:07.520 position:63%
To remove the impurities it has.

00:34:07.520 --> 00:34:14.520 position:63%
It comes out with the rope so that it is detached.

00:34:15.080 --> 00:34:15.840 position:63%
It will be dissolving.

00:34:28.240 --> 00:34:30.480 position:63%
Now we're going to add gasoline.

00:34:33.320 --> 00:34:36.600 position:63%
I don't know if the bulls who consume it see the process, would they dare...

00:34:36.680 --> 00:34:37.680 position:63%
To consume it.

00:34:37.680 --> 00:34:38.880 position:63%
To consume it, right?

00:34:42.000 --> 00:34:42.240 position:63%
Sure.

00:34:42.240 --> 00:34:42.840 position:63%
Do you consume it?

00:34:43.120 --> 00:34:46.040 position:63%
No, sir.

00:34:46.160 --> 00:34:46.280 position:63%
No.

00:34:47.240 --> 00:34:47.360 position:63%
No.

00:34:47.400 --> 00:34:48.120 position:63%
Why not?

00:34:48.120 --> 00:34:48.760 position:63%
I don't know.

00:34:48.800 --> 00:34:52.240 position:63%
Maybe if you see the process, you'll see what it has.

00:34:52.240 --> 00:34:53.960 position:63%
And you say, no, this is poison, no, no.

00:34:54.480 --> 00:34:54.600 position:63%
No.

00:35:06.560 --> 00:35:09.760 position:63%
Once it's free of impurities, they have to dry the coca paste.

00:35:11.240 --> 00:35:15.920 position:63%
And we're surprised to see that drug traffickers use conventional spin dryers for this.

00:35:29.600 --> 00:35:34.360 position:63%
The second part of the process consists of turning this clean coca paste into cocaine.

00:35:59.760 --> 00:36:04.560 position:63%
So that the yellowish powder doesn't come out.

00:36:04.560 --> 00:36:06.960 position:63%
It has to be totally white.

00:36:06.960 --> 00:36:08.320 position:63%
Otherwise it loses a lot of pressure.

00:36:21.920 --> 00:36:24.000 position:63%
The process reaches the final stage.

00:36:26.200 --> 00:36:28.720 position:63%
They add the last chemical products to the mixture.

00:36:30.120 --> 00:36:31.880 position:63%
And they only have to wait for it to boil.

00:36:50.480 --> 00:36:51.600 position:63%
Look, you can see the cut.

00:36:51.600 --> 00:36:52.800 position:63%
This that will appear here will be cocaine.

00:36:53.160 --> 00:36:53.640 position:63%
Cocaine.

00:36:53.640 --> 00:36:55.240 position:63%
The liquid will appear solid.

00:36:55.400 --> 00:36:55.840 position:63%
Solid, solid, yes.

00:36:56.200 --> 00:36:57.760 position:63%
Like a flour.

00:36:57.760 --> 00:36:58.200 position:63%
A flour.

00:36:58.200 --> 00:37:00.360 position:63%
There comes the cocaine.

00:37:02.160 --> 00:37:03.160 position:63%
There is all the cocaine.

00:37:03.160 --> 00:37:05.800 position:63%
After what?

00:37:05.880 --> 00:37:06.240 position:63%
Eight hours?

00:37:06.240 --> 00:37:06.920 position:63%
Eight hours.

00:37:07.240 --> 00:37:10.040 position:63%
Eight hours later.

00:37:10.040 --> 00:37:13.640 position:63%
The cocaine.

00:37:18.080 --> 00:37:22.200 position:63%
The drums of cocaine are emptied to filter and eliminate the chemical remainders.

00:37:33.080 --> 00:37:35.720 position:63%
The only thing that remains to be done is pressing it.

00:37:42.640 --> 00:37:45.680 position:63%
And drying.

00:37:55.800 --> 00:38:00.680 position:63%
25 kilos of cocaine drying in a microwave in the middle of the jungle.

00:38:05.960 --> 00:38:07.440 position:63%
The cocaine is ready.

00:38:23.080 --> 00:38:25.800 position:63%
We continue following the trail of Colombian cocaine.

00:38:26.760 --> 00:38:30.040 position:63%
If production has fragmented, so has its transportation.

00:38:32.800 --> 00:38:37.640 position:63%
Drug traffickers get around police pressure by smuggling the drug into all the neighbouring countries.

00:38:39.400 --> 00:38:47.440 position:63%
And from these countries, cocaine travels and reaches the hands of Mexican cartels, the new lords and masters of drug trafficking.

00:38:48.320 --> 00:38:54.400 position:63%
And among the Mexican cartels, there is one that is considered the largest drug trafficking cartel in the world.

00:38:55.200 --> 00:38:56.360 position:63%
The Sinaloa cartel.

00:39:32.720 --> 00:39:34.360 position:63%
Colombia.

00:39:34.400 --> 00:39:36.360 position:63%
It's coming up little by little through Central America.

00:39:37.400 --> 00:39:39.560 position:63%
We received it here in Sinaloa.

00:39:40.800 --> 00:39:43.440 position:63%
We prepared it and sent it to the United States.

00:39:52.000 --> 00:39:57.240 position:63%
Let's play with numbers a little bit just to understand what we are about to witness.

00:39:58.880 --> 00:39:59.960 position:63%
400 kilos.

00:40:00.600 --> 00:40:06.680 position:63%
...Of cocaine here in Sinaloa worth around 8 million dollars.

00:40:07.480 --> 00:40:16.120 position:63%
But if they reach the states and they are sold in the streets, we're talking about more than 70 million dollars.

00:40:47.160 --> 00:40:49.680 position:63%
And now?

00:40:49.680 --> 00:40:50.720 position:63%
Are you going to wait?

00:40:50.720 --> 00:40:53.440 position:63%
No, I'm going to wait.

00:40:53.440 --> 00:40:54.880 position:63%
I'm going to eat lunch.

00:40:54.880 --> 00:40:55.320 position:63%
Or I'll go to the market.

00:41:02.720 --> 00:41:06.120 position:63%
The drug traffickers confirm the position and the time of delivery.

00:41:07.240 --> 00:41:10.960 position:63%
Come on, get in.

00:41:10.960 --> 00:41:11.640 position:63%
You're all right.

00:41:19.560 --> 00:41:26.440 position:63%
The boat is about to arrive and the cartel men prepare the vehicle to load 400 kilos of cocaine.

00:41:32.040 --> 00:41:35.520 position:63%
Everything must be ready to unload the shipment in the shortest time possible.

00:41:36.320 --> 00:41:39.600 position:63%
But at the last moment, it looks like something unexpected arises.

00:41:53.080 --> 00:42:00.040 position:63%
400 kilos of cocaine in sight on a small boat, which seems to befit fishermen rather than drug traffickers.

00:42:50.480 --> 00:42:55.560 position:63%
Once the unloading has been completed, the only thing that remains to be done is checking the merchandise.

00:43:04.760 --> 00:43:50.560 position:63%
The seal they were expecting to see From a trustworthy Colombian producer The whole operation is done in less than four minutes Oh And where is that going now?

00:43:50.560 --> 00:43:53.520 position:63%
It's going to a security house.

00:43:53.600 --> 00:43:55.240 position:63%
They've been there for a while.

00:43:55.240 --> 00:43:57.360 position:63%
While they're preparing it, they're sending it.

00:43:57.360 --> 00:43:58.160 position:63%
To send it to the United States?

00:43:58.160 --> 00:44:01.960 position:63%
That's right.

00:44:01.960 --> 00:44:04.040 position:63%
Cocaine burns people's hands.

00:44:04.720 --> 00:44:09.800 position:63%
The longer it's exposed, the higher the risk of being caught by surprise by the security forces.

00:44:12.920 --> 00:44:15.960 position:63%
And the higher the risk of being assaulted by a rival gang.

00:44:23.840 --> 00:44:28.800 position:63%
A merchandise whose estimated value is 70 million euros is too powerful a lure.

00:44:30.280 --> 00:44:33.720 position:63%
Hence the importance of safe houses to hide the drug shipment.

00:44:45.800 --> 00:44:48.560 position:63%
We arrive at a small construction in the middle of nowhere.

00:44:51.600 --> 00:44:53.080 position:63%
A hiding place for cocaine.

00:45:10.600 --> 00:45:26.200 position:63%
Thanks for watching The process will continue now.

00:45:26.320 --> 00:45:30.400 position:63%
Do they have to repackage them or what do they have to do?

00:45:30.480 --> 00:45:32.600 position:63%
We're going to do another maneuver.

00:45:32.600 --> 00:45:32.720 position:63%
Why?

00:45:33.880 --> 00:45:34.600 position:63%
Well, it depends.

00:45:34.600 --> 00:45:37.120 position:63%
Maybe it's because of the water.

00:45:37.160 --> 00:45:38.040 position:63%
To protect the sea.

00:45:39.440 --> 00:45:40.720 position:63%
Ah, because of the water from the sea?

00:45:40.720 --> 00:45:40.840 position:63%
Yes.

00:45:44.080 --> 00:45:48.600 position:63%
The value of cocaine increases with each stage and every precaution must be taken.

00:45:51.760 --> 00:45:53.840 position:63%
And this is ready to be used in the United States?

00:45:53.920 --> 00:45:56.760 position:63%
That's right.

00:45:58.960 --> 00:46:02.800 position:63%
The Colombian cocaine is kept safely and ready to take the last step.

00:46:04.160 --> 00:46:06.600 position:63%
The trip from Sinaloa to the USA.

00:46:16.200 --> 00:46:17.000 position:63%
Two days later.

00:46:17.880 --> 00:46:21.080 position:63%
Felipe tells us that the drug dispatch operation is ready.

00:46:23.280 --> 00:46:29.440 position:63%
A hundred out of the 400 kilos of cocaine that are kept in the safe house are about to be dispatched by sea.

00:46:50.400 --> 00:46:54.440 position:63%
At a point on the way, we come across a still vehicle on the ditch.

00:47:19.360 --> 00:47:23.720 position:63%
As soon as we get in, we discover this one is transporting the drug shipment.

00:47:50.400 --> 00:47:55.560 position:63%
The plan is to load the cocaine into a boat that will take it to the USA border.

00:47:56.800 --> 00:47:59.760 position:63%
But heavy rains are making the operation more difficult.

00:48:13.720 --> 00:48:16.360 position:63%
The drug traffickers must improvise a solution.

00:49:33.880 --> 00:49:39.080 position:63%
We arrive at the point that has been agreed and everything is done with perfect coordination.

00:49:42.680 --> 00:49:47.200 position:63%
The small boat has just arrived and the drug traffickers are going to load the cocaine.

00:50:38.760 --> 00:50:41.040 position:63%
The operation has been completed successfully.

00:50:48.360 --> 00:50:53.000 position:63%
A hundred more kilos of Colombian cocaine are dispatched to the USA.

00:50:57.640 --> 00:51:04.120 position:63%
A hundred kilos of cocaine that show how the drug trafficking business has transformed in order to survive.

00:51:06.560 --> 00:51:10.160 position:63%
How a cartel from Medellin is replaced by the Gulf cartel.

00:51:11.760 --> 00:51:20.960 position:63%
And how the Gulf cartel, cornered, is replaced by hundreds of small organizations that are prepared to satisfy an incessant demand.

00:51:26.360 --> 00:51:30.360 position:63%
The Mexican cartels have played a crucial role in this transformation.

00:51:31.960 --> 00:51:41.920 position:63%
If Colombia produces the product and the USA buys it, the Mexican cartels are responsible for placing the orders and for bringing the cocaine to the table of the consumer.

00:51:43.920 --> 00:51:46.720 position:63%
A new order that follows the same good old laws.

00:51:49.080 --> 00:51:50.880 position:63%
The laws of supply and demand.

00:51:53.400 --> 00:51:55.480 position:63%
And it continues charging the same price.

00:51:58.120 --> 00:52:04.360 position:63%
The blood of traffickers, consumers, and of those who fight drug trafficking.

00:52:06.840 --> 00:52:13.400 position:63%
25 years after the death of Pablo Escobar, cocaine continues being the king of drugs.

